1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:03,741
Let's sink to the bottom of the ocean.

2
00:00:03,811 --> 00:00:05,585
Two hundred metres.

3
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:09,104
Almost all the sunlight is already gone.

4
00:00:09,174 --> 00:00:11,745
Three hundred and thirty-two.

5
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:17,257
The deepest anyone has ever gone on scuba.

6
00:00:17,329 --> 00:00:18,871
One thousand.

7
00:00:18,954 --> 00:00:20,820
Total darkness.

8
00:00:20,953 --> 00:00:25,368
From here on, the only light is made by animals.

9
00:00:25,438 --> 00:00:27,112
Nearly three thousand.

10
00:00:27,387 --> 00:00:31,406
A Cuvier's beaked whale was tracked diving this deep.

11
00:00:31,456 --> 00:00:32,816
On one breath.

12
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:35,164
Three thousand eight hundred.

13
00:00:35,247 --> 00:00:36,870
The Titanic.

14
00:00:36,945 --> 00:00:38,456
Four thousand.

15
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:39,860
The abyss.

16
00:00:40,135 --> 00:00:45,868
Near freezing, and four hundred times the pressure at the surface.

17
00:00:45,938 --> 00:00:49,307
Eight thousand three hundred and thirty-six.

18
00:00:49,391 --> 00:00:51,932
The deepest fish ever filmed.

19
00:00:52,066 --> 00:00:54,849
A little snailfish, just swimming.

20
00:00:54,919 --> 00:00:57,490
Almost eleven thousand metres.

21
00:00:57,766 --> 00:00:59,671
The Challenger Deep.

22
00:01:00,128 --> 00:01:03,189
Fewer people have been here than to space.

23
00:01:03,639 --> 00:01:07,189
And down here, someone already found...

24
00:01:07,324 --> 00:01:09,302
a plastic bag.
